    "section_evoo_v3_faq_rRJhLR": {
      "type": "section-evoo-v3-faq",
      "blocks": {
        "faq_item_BFc6Am": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What makes Olive Aura different from any other \"extra virgin\" olive oil on the shelf?",
            "answer": "<p>Most olive oils sit 6–24 hours before pressing enough time for oxidation to quietly begin. Olive Aura goes from harvest to cold-press in under 3 hours. That's not a marketing line; it's a process decision that preserves polyphenols, natural flavour, and low acidity that cheaper brands simply can't replicate. Every lot is also independently lab-tested scan the QR code and read the actual Certificate of Analysis yourself.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_pgG9dR": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "The label says \"cold-pressed.\" Isn't that standard? Why does it matter here?",
            "answer": "<p>Cold-pressed\" is widely misused. Many brands heat the olives to 35–40 °C during extraction to improve yield  which destroys the delicate polyphenols responsible for that signature peppery finish and most of the antioxidant activity. Olive Aura maintains temperatures below 27 °C throughout the entire process true cold extraction, verified by independent labs under NATA accreditation and AOCS standards. True Cold Extraction · &lt;27 °C</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_zet6LP": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How do I know the polyphenol content is actually high and not just a claim?",
            "answer": "<p>You verify it. Olive Aura is triple-tested by NABL-accredited independent laboratories  not in-house quality checks. Every bottle carries a QR code linked to the actual Certificate of Analysis for that lot. Over 70% polyphenol content and more than 80% oleic acid these are measurable values, not estimates. Polyphenols are the compounds that help reduce oxidative stress and support healthy inflammatory responses in the body. NABL Lab-Verified · QR-Traceable</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_Q6TUxh": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Is this oil blended with cheaper imports? How do I know it's 100% Australian?",
            "answer": "<p>Olive Aura is single-origin sourced exclusively from Australian groves, never blended with cheaper bulk imports or refined oils. Blending is a common industry practice used to reduce costs, but it dilutes polyphenol levels and masks inferior quality. What's in the bottle is pure fruit expression: 100% cold-pressed Australian extra virgin olive oil nothing added, nothing corrected, nothing hidden.<br/>Single-Origin · No Blending</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_WyBt4K": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Does the packaging actually protect the oil's quality, or is that just branding?",
            "answer": "<p>Olive oil's three enemies are light, heat, and oxygen. Olive Aura's packaging counters all three: dark-tinted bottles block UV light, cool-chain storage maintains temperature integrity from grove to shelf, and nitrogen flushing replaces oxygen in the bottle before sealing preventing oxidation before you even open it. This level of post-extraction care is rare, and it's why Olive Aura retains its bright, clean, peppery flavour until the last drop. Nitrogen-Flushed · Dark-Glass · Cool-Chain</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_TGrNaL": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Why should I use olive oil specifically for heart health isn't all cooking oil the same?",
            "answer": "<p>Far from it. Olive Aura contains 68.5% monounsaturated fat (MUFA) the well-researched heart-healthy fat associated with supporting healthy cholesterol levels and reducing oxidative stress. Most refined cooking oils are high in omega-6 polyunsaturated fats that can contribute to inflammation when consumed in excess. Olive Aura is also low in saturated fat. Combined with its polyphenol content, it supports cardiovascular health, energy metabolism, and overall well-being making it liquid nutrition, not just a cooking medium. 68.5% MUFA · Heart-Healthy Fats Freshness you can measure. Purity you can trust.</p>"
          }
        }
